  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Zonisamide is an anticonvulsant used to treat epilepsy, including focal seizures, and has also been studied for Parkinson's disease and migraine. It is an approved medicine, authorised in the European Union for epilepsy, and used alongside other approved and investigational uses.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q219957&quot;>Wikidata Q219957</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>zonisamide</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>N03AX15</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB00909&quot;>DB00909</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/5734&quot;>5734</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:10127&quot;>10127</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q219957&quot;>Q219957</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C8H8N2O3S</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>212.223 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
